      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-derived alumina scale remains coherent and stable during exposure above 900 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al oxidizes preferentially because Al2O3 has high thermodynamic stability relative to competing oxides.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9026100::web::022::cross_section_observation_of_oxide_layer"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al2O3 has low ionic or cationic mobility and therefore grows more slowly than chromia or mixed oxides.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC9692591::web::026::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous alumina scale acts as a diffusion barrier that limits subsequent cation and oxygen transport.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC9692591::web::026::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slow alumina growth produces a coherent, fine-grained oxide scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alumina scale minimizes thermal-stress-induced cracking and spallation relative to an Al-free alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al concentration governs oxidation kinetics and whether a protective Al2O3 layer forms instead of a less-protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9692591::web::026::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A minor, optimized Al addition can preserve the alloy's phase stability while still supplying enough Al to form protective alumina.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Homogeneous Al distribution enables selective formation of the protective alumina scale.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al depletion associated with alumina formation can cause structural instability in the underlying alloy.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "An Al-free CrFeCoNi HEA typically develops unstable mixed oxide scales above 900 °C.",
